**Reused evidence**
REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0007"],"lenses":["2B.10"]}
Sharif entered office through a constitutional crisis and a turbulent coalition context, which matters for baseline but does not itself show external conduct.

REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0008"],"lenses":["2B.3","2B.8","2B.10"]}
Reuters’ pre-accession analysis still matters for attribution: Sharif was expected to work within military-dominant foreign and defense structures and would not have full independence.

REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0009"],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7"]}
Sharif’s April 2022 letter to Modi is direct peace-oriented conduct and one of the cleanest India-facing evidence points.

REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0010"],"lenses":["2B.10"]}
The March 2022 missile accident is inherited crisis context for 2022, not Sharif’s act, but it shaped the starting security environment.

REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0011"],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
The Islamabad Declaration is useful as official crisis-response context after the missile incident and for Pakistan’s stated restraint posture.

REUSE_JSON: {"evidence_ids":["E0013"],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
MOFA’s later statement on the missile incident reinforces the same restraint-and-joint-probe line.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNGA adopts resolution calling for lasting peace in Ukraine; Pakistan abstains","publisher":"Associated Press of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.app.com.pk/global/unga-adopts-resolution-calling-for-lasting-peace-in-ukraine-pakistan-abstains-2/","claim":"Pakistan abstained on a Ukraine resolution while its UN ambassador called for de-escalation, renewed negotiations, and sustained dialogue for a peaceful diplomatic solution, while backing respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity.","locator":"article body, explanation-of-vote section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official state newswire quoting Pakistan’s UN explanation of vote; strong for attribution and dated policy posture.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 Ukraine-war diplomacy context.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Pakistan’s diplomatic line under Sharif, though not a personal operational order.","contrary_evidence":["Pakistan abstained rather than co-sponsoring a condemnation, which shows caution and balancing rather than maximal alignment with the anti-Russia camp."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"War in Ukraine reflects ‘failure of diplomacy’ — Pakistan PM","publisher":"Arab News Pakistan / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-04-30","url":"https://www.arabnews.pk/node/2073721/pakistan","claim":"Sharif said the Ukraine war reflected a failure of diplomacy and called for immediate cessation of hostilities, sustained dialogue, and a diplomatic solution in line with international law and the UN Charter.","locator":"interview paragraphs 89-100","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-syndicated written interview with direct quotes from Sharif; good attribution, though still secondary reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and about an active international war.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Sharif rhetoric and diplomatic positioning.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is diplomatic rhetoric, not proof of concrete mediation success.","Pakistan continued to balance relations with Moscow and Kyiv rather than align fully with sanctions diplomacy."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan willing to play positive role to bridge US-China differences: PM","publisher":"Radio Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-08-17","url":"https://www.radio.gov.pk/17-08-2022/pakistan-willing-to-play-a-positive-role-to-bridge-the-us-china-differences-pm","claim":"Sharif said Pakistan wanted to help bridge US-China differences for world peace and stability, warned against confrontational bloc politics, and said Pakistan sought good relations with neighbors through peaceful dispute resolution and international law.","locator":"article body paragraphs 33-46","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official broadcaster reproducing the PM’s own interview remarks with clear dated attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Sharif statement; useful for peace orientation and for distinguishing his public line from inherited strategic constraints.","contrary_evidence":["The remarks are broad foreign-policy framing, not a specific peace settlement or operational restraint decision."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PM reiterates resolve to provide assistance to Afghan people","publisher":"Radio Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-24","url":"https://www.radio.gov.pk/24-06-2022/pm-reiterates-resolve-to-provide-assistance-to-afghan-people","claim":"After speaking with the Afghan interim prime minister, Sharif promised continued support after the Afghan earthquake, said border crossings were opened for injured Afghans, and said Pakistan wanted stronger bilateral ties to promote peace, progress, and prosperity.","locator":"article body paragraphs 1-7","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official broadcaster summary of a direct PM interaction with clear humanitarian and bilateral-language attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 regional-security and humanitarian context.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Sharif conduct in crisis diplomacy and humanitarian facilitation.","contrary_evidence":["Humanitarian assistance does not by itself resolve the underlying cross-border militant and border-security disputes."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"All-out measures at border crossing points in place to facilitate Afghans","publisher":"Radio Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-12-10","url":"https://www.radio.gov.pk/10-12-2022/all-out-measures-at-border-crossing-points-in-place-to-facilitate-afghans","claim":"Pakistan said it had taken facilitative measures at all five Afghanistan border crossings to keep movement smooth for pedestrians, patients, traders, tourists, and transporters.","locator":"article body paragraphs 36-43","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official broadcaster summary with concrete border-management details and operational context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 border-management context.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to the Sharif government’s border posture, though it is administrative rather than a high-level peace bargain.","contrary_evidence":["Border facilitation sits alongside contemporaneous border clashes and does not erase them."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"OIC Secretary-General Held Discussions with the New Prime Minister of Pakistan","publisher":"Organisation of Islamic Cooperation","publication_date":"2022-04-29","url":"https://www.oic-oci.org/en/news/1306","claim":"At Sharif’s first major OIC engagement, discussions centered on Palestine, Afghanistan, Jammu and Kashmir, and Islamophobia, and the two sides emphasized cooperation among member states and support for Pakistan’s chairmanship agenda.","locator":"article body paragraphs 87-90","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official multilateral record of a dated meeting involving the PM and OIC leadership.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 diplomatic context.","ruler_attribution":"Direct diplomatic engagement by Sharif, but still a multilateral agenda-setting event rather than a conflict decision.","contrary_evidence":["The OIC is a declaratory forum; the source does not show binding conflict resolution or enforcement."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan looks for peace with all its neighbours including India: PM Shehbaz at UN","publisher":"The Indian Express","publication_date":"2022-09-24","url":"https://indianexpress.com/article/world/pakistan-looks-for-peace-with-all-its-neighbours-including-india-pm-shehbaz-at-un-8169404/","claim":"At the UN General Assembly, Sharif said Pakistan sought peace with all neighbors, including India, but argued that durable peace and stability in South Asia depended on a just and lasting Kashmir settlement.","locator":"article body and quoted UNGA speech excerpt","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"PTI-sourced reporting on a live UN speech, with direct quoted language but still secondary reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 UNGA speech period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Sharif diplomacy and public justification strategy.","contrary_evidence":["The Kashmir linkage makes the peace offer conditional, not unconditional.","India treated the speech as old-pattern rhetoric rather than a breakthrough."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Six Pakistanis, one Afghan soldier killed in cross-border clash","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","publication_date":"2022-12-12","url":"https://theprint.in/world/six-pakistanis-one-afghan-soldier-killed-in-cross-border-clash-2/1261178/","claim":"Cross-border shelling and gunfire at Chaman killed Pakistani civilians and one Afghan soldier; Sharif condemned the deaths as unfortunate and said the Afghan interim government should ensure such incidents were not repeated.","locator":"lead and closing quoted statement","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with direct incident description and a clear PM response statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 border-crisis period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Sharif’s crisis response, though not necessarily to initiating the clash.","contrary_evidence":["Pakistan said Afghan forces fired first; Afghanistan gave a different account, so the initiating role is contested.","The episode shows that restraint was not complete and that deadly border violence still occurred under Sharif."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Taliban authorities summon Pakistan’s envoy to protest 'military strikes'","publisher":"The Express Tribune / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-04-16","url":"https://tribune.com.pk/story/2352901/afghan-taliban-summon-pakistans-envoy-to-protest-military-strikes?amp=1","claim":"Afghan authorities protested alleged Pakistani military strikes inside Afghanistan, while Pakistan denied the strikes and said the two countries discussed border issues and resolution through diplomacy.","locator":"Reuters report body and quoted Afghan foreign ministry statement","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-based report on a serious allegation and denial, but the underlying operational facts remain contested.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact April 2022 period, immediately after Sharif took office.","ruler_attribution":"Potentially relevant to Sharif-era conduct, but attribution is weak because Pakistan denied the allegation and the report does not show a direct PM order.","contrary_evidence":["The allegation is not independently adjudicated here.","Because Pakistan denied involvement, this is best treated as contested contrary evidence rather than settled fact."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.4","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan says cross-border attacks from Afghanistan have increased","publisher":"Reuters via MarketScreener","publication_date":"2022-04-17","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Pakistan-says-cross-border-attacks-from-Afghanistan-have-increased-40074954/","claim":"Pakistan said incidents targeting its security forces from Afghanistan had risen significantly and urged Taliban authorities to act against militants, following the alleged air-strike episode and rising border tension.","locator":"Reuters report lead and foreign-office quote","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire on a live border-security dispute with direct official attribution, though it remains one side’s framing of the problem.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 border-security context.","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to the Sharif government’s posture on Afghan-border security, but still more a state response than a clearly ruler-authored decision.","contrary_evidence":["This is a complaint about incoming attacks, not proof of Pakistani aggression.","It highlights tension and insecurity rather than a peace breakthrough."],"lenses":["2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan abstains on UNGA resolution voicing concern over volatility in Afghanistan since Taliban Takeover","publisher":"Associated Press of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-11-11","url":"https://www.app.com.pk/global/pakistan-abstains-on-unga-resolution-voicing-concern-over-volatility-in-afghanistan-since-taliban-takeover/","claim":"Pakistan abstained on an Afghanistan resolution, called it unbalanced and unrealistic, but also pressed for engagement with the Taliban authorities, unfreezing Afghan reserves, and better handling of TTP references and OIC roles.","locator":"article body, explanation-of-vote section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official state newswire reporting Pakistan’s exact explanation of vote and policy preference for engagement rather than isolation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 Afghan-policy context.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Pakistan’s Sharif-era diplomatic line, though not to a single personal decision.","contrary_evidence":["The abstention shows caution and balance rather than a strong alignment with the resolution’s harsher language.","Pakistan’s own complaint about omitted TTP language shows its security lens remained active."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PM congratulates President Erdogan over Ukraine grain deal","publisher":"Associated Press of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-07-23","url":"https://www.app.com.pk/global/pm-congratulates-president-erdogan-over-ukraine-grain-deal/","claim":"Sharif called the Russia-Ukraine grain deal a historic victory of diplomacy and said major crises could be averted through meaningful engagement.","locator":"article body and embedded tweet excerpt","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official newswire reproducing the PM’s public reaction and direct social-media wording.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 Russia-Ukraine diplomacy context.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Sharif public diplomacy signal.","contrary_evidence":["This is praise for a diplomatic breakthrough, not evidence that Sharif himself mediated the deal.","It is a general pro-diplomacy statement rather than a country-specific settlement record."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across UN, OIC, APP, Radio Pakistan, Reuters syndications, Dawn, Indian Express, Arab News, ThePrint, Express Tribune, Al Jazeera, RFE/RL, SCMP, and a few later retrospectives.

I rejected or deprioritized items that were:
- duplicates of the same Reuters wire on the March 2022 missile accident or the December 2022 Chaman clash,
- out of period or too retrospective when a 2022 source existed,
- generic explainers that repeated the same facts without better attribution,
- blocked/cache-miss pages that added no usable text,
- domestic political stories that did not bear on external conduct,
- reports on other leaders or later 2024-2026 events that were not Sharif-in-2022 evidence.

I also kept the local prior as the baseline:
- the structured 2022 prior shows no internationalized conflict events or fatalities for Pakistan, so this chapter is mostly about diplomacy, border management, and disputed border incidents rather than a major interstate war.

**Remaining gaps**
- There is still no direct evidence that Sharif personally ordered, blocked, or reoriented any Pakistan military operation abroad in 2022.
- The April 2022 Afghanistan air-strike allegation remains contested; I found reporting on the accusation and denial, but not a settled independent finding.
- I did not find a clean 2022 record of formal ceasefire negotiation output with India beyond public diplomacy and the Kashmir/peace messaging.
- Proxy-control evidence remains thin. The record shows concern about Afghanistan/TTP and border violence, but not a demonstrable Sharif-level command decision over proxies.
- The military’s practical role in foreign and defense policy remains partially opaque, so attribution is stronger for public diplomacy than for hard security conduct.

If you want, I can next turn this into a tight chapter-brief focused only on the strongest 2B positive/negative evidence and the attribution conclusion.
